    },
    "meaning": "yes (contradicting a no); but; do (for emphasis)",
    "shortDefinition": "Yes after a negative question; however; softens or stresses."
  },
  "intro": {
    "title": "The word English doesn't have",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Doch is the 'yes' you use to contradict a negative: Kommst du nicht? – Doch! (Yes, I am!). Ja would sound like you agree with the 'not'.",
      "It also means 'but, however', and it's a softener in requests and commands: Komm doch mit! (Oh, come along!). Setz dich doch! (Do sit down!)."
    ]
  },
